              "correctAnswer": 0,
              "explanation": "McCabe's formula is V(G) = E - N + 2P. With E = 14, N = 10, and P = 1: V(G) = 14 - 10 + 2(1) = 6. This establishes the exact minimum number of test cases required for complete basis path coverage."
